.TH APP:QUOTA 1 "July 2026" "SPP WebOS" "SPP Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
app:quota \- Configure hardware resource boundaries (RAM/CPU) for WebOS Guest Apps.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php app:quota
.I alias
[\-\-ram=\fIlimit\fR]
[\-\-cpu=\fIseconds\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B app:quota
command configures strict hardware limits for legacy or third-party Guest Apps running under the SPP WebOS Hypervisor. 
By utilizing the SPP Kernel ResourceManager, it prevents unstable guest applications from consuming excessive memory or CPU time, thereby preventing system-wide crashes (Fault Isolation). If an app exceeds its allocated quota, the Kernel gracefully kills the thread and throws a WebOsKernelPanicException.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR alias
The unique IAM identifier assigned to the guest app during installation (e.g., wordpress:blog). This argument is required.
.TP
.BR \-\-ram=\fIlimit\fR
Sets the maximum RAM allocation allowed for the instance, formatted as a standard PHP memory string (e.g., 128M, 1G).
.TP
.BR \-\-cpu=\fIseconds\fR
Sets the maximum execution time in seconds allowed for a single thread spawned by the instance (e.g., 10s, 30s).
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.B Filesystem Writes:
The command writes the quota definitions directly into the centralized WebOS YAML Registry.
.PP
.B Kernel Interception:
During execution, the SPP ResourceManager dynamically applies \fBini_set('memory_limit')\fR and \fBset_time_limit()\fR before handing control to the guest app.
